  "method": {
    "feed": "Steel from one source chest, water supplied only to the water and shell inlets. Ordinary pipe connections between all machines. Unrestricted oxygen drainage. Five yellow inserters deliver steel, raw pellets, formed pellets, shells and sealed output. A single external source holds the grid at full power. Neither setup preloads intermediates or uses run-pacing logic.",
    "measurement": "Two equal-inventory snapshots after startup with matched material flows. Exports already counted at the start of the interval are excluded. Export timestamps are polled every 15 ticks, 60 ticks per game second. Electrical draw is the difference between cumulative energy delivered by the dedicated power source divided by the number of exports. Native fluid statistics and measured intermediate-inventory changes distinguish processing from storage.",
    "power_scope": "All attached machines and inserters, including powered idle drain. Excludes mining, steelmaking, water/oxygen infrastructure and reactor logistics. Gross fuel-equivalent power assumes adequate reactor load and generation capacity."
